    "observations": [
      "Writer timing includes input JSON decode, original JSON encode, lifecycle auditing, frame/raw/file hashes and final close. It excludes computing or hashing original DUT packet/result payloads; digest strings are replayed as data.",
      "One fixed-order sample per arm, with original first, cannot establish a stable CPU benefit or full-DUT speedup. Write-call reduction is established by retained counters and source mechanism.",
      "Accepted bytes/events/hashes can describe only RAM; persisted counters/hash describe a known OS-acknowledged prefix, not fsync or power-loss durability. Raised writes correctly retain a lower-bound prefix and do not retry.",
      "The two buffered sudden-exit controls retain only the header, losing 1214 accepted bytes. This is a material weakening of failed-run evidence retention; do not present buffered/unbuffered crash evidence as equivalent.",
      "Original real-prefix files remain without END. The successful footer control is a synthetic one-group sequence, not DUT lifecycle or numerical PASS.",
      "Existing diagnostics do not cover failed-drain-during-append, fsync failure, actual SIGKILL or signal delivery. No extra tests were performed in this review.",
      "35 unique declared records and preserved outputs support one execution per declared case in the harness; they are not a system-wide proof that no other process ran."
    ],
